   "text": {
    "L1": "A happy school is clean, green and safe, and everyone helps to care for it.",
    "L2": "The sweeper is not the only person responsible. Students, teachers and staff must all avoid litter and tidy up.",
    "L3": "Wet waste, such as peels and food scraps, goes into the green bin.",
    "L4": "Wet waste can become dark, crumbly compost with help from microbes and earthworms.",
    "L5": "Dry waste, such as paper, plastic and cans, goes into the blue bin for recycling.",
    "L6": "Plastic does not rot in a compost pit, so it must stay with the dry waste.",
    "L7": "We can save water by closing taps, reporting leaks and collecting rain from the roof.",
    "L8": "Trees give shade, clean water and soap support safety, and we should never run on stairs."
   },
